      "text": "To determine after how many bounces the ball first rises to a height less than 30 cm, we need to calculate the height of each bounce and observe the pattern.\n\n1. **Initial Drop:**\n   The ball is initially dropped from a height of 243 cm.\n\n2. **First Bounce:**\n   The ball bounces back to \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) of the initial height.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Height after first bounce} = 243 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = 162 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Second Bounce:**\n   The ball bounces back to \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) of the height from the first bounce.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Height after second bounce} = 162 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = 108 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Third Bounce:**\n   The ball bounces back to \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) of the height from the second bounce.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Height after third bounce} = 108 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = 72 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Fourth Bounce:**\n   The ball bounces back to \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) of the height from the third bounce.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Height after fourth bounce} = 72 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = 48 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Fifth Bounce:**\n   The ball bounces back to \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) of the height from the fourth bounce.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Height after fifth bounce} = 48 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = 32 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\nAt the fifth bounce, the height of the ball is 32 cm, which is less than 30 cm. Therefore, the ball first rises to a height less than 30 cm after the fifth bounce.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{5}\n\\]",
